  "reason": "Evidence: config_003 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieved 0.725 acc, far outperforming scgpt-based configs (~0.52). The only other tested fusion variant (config_015, scgpt+concat) was ~1.3 pts below its weighted counterpart (config_048), suggesting weighted fusion may be important but the gap was small. Question: Does the fusion method (weighted vs concat) matter when paired with the superior scvi_n200 encoder? config_046 changes only fusion from weighted to concat while keeping all other settings identical to the current best (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, multiprofile). This is the cleanest single-variable ablation against the best config, giving unambiguous evidence about whether weighted fusion is a meaningful lever or whether concat is equally effective. With 5 experiments remaining, resolving this design choice early informs whether to focus subsequent budget on image encoder or aggregation variations."
}

